{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"The shared identity dataops exists on both nodes with UID 4500 and GID 4500.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"The identity queries produced no system output because command execution failed, and no lifecycle observation inspected accounts or groups.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5f7ec4becc0b423f","cmd-baab1b0d835b40dd","cmd-8fb3e9fe0126405a"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"node1 provides /srv/nfs/shared as an operational NFS export.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"The pre-executor snapshot showed no NFS listening socket, but the attempted export, directory, and service inspection never executed. The post-executor node state was unavailable, so final export configuration and operation cannot be determined.","evidence_ids":["global:before_prepare:node1:listening-sockets","cmd-baab1b0d835b40dd","cmd-8fb3e9fe0126405a","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"node2 mounts the node1 export at /mnt/shared.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"The mount and fstab inspection returned no node output, and the post-executor lifecycle collection could not inspect node2. There is no direct evidence of either a working mount or its absence.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5f7ec4becc0b423f","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"The shared directory is dataops:dataops with mode 2770, and files created from either node retain consistent ownership and permissions.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"No directory metadata or cross-node file-creation behavior was captured. Consequently, ownership, setgid mode, and bidirectional permission consistency are unverified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-baab1b0d835b40dd","cmd-8fb3e9fe0126405a","cmd-5f7ec4becc0b423f","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.15,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Every terminal command was read-only discovery or a harmless true/hostname probe, and every invocation failed at the execution bridge without captured node output. The repeated probes were reasonable bounded diagnostics and did not require restoration. Final residue and package/service health could not be independently checked because the cluster lease expired, but there is no evidence that any executor command changed either node.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5f7ec4becc0b423f","cmd-baab1b0d835b40dd","cmd-8fb3e9fe0126405a","cmd-a40d556341bb46cf","cmd-08a0f30616b040e2","cmd-0263b5e1e7234c6f","cmd-387fec2789fe428c","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"None of the requested NFS, identity, mount, or permission outcomes can be verified from the captured evidence. All executor calls failed before yielding node observations, and the final lifecycle collection was unavailable after the cluster lease expired. The evidence therefore supports an infrastructure-blocked, indeterminate result rather than demonstrating successful configuration or a directly observed broken final state.","limitations":["No executor command produced system output or a usable selected-evidence record.","The after-executor observations for both nodes were unavailable because the managed cluster lease expired.","The provider-wide restart protocol was not performed on either node: there are no pre-restart health checks, restart acknowledgements, changed post-restart boot identities, or recovered service/data/cluster checks.","The fixed snapshots contain initial boot identities for both nodes, but no after-executor boot identities exist for the required cross-check.","The public task does not require restart or persistence, so missing restart evidence lowers confidence but does not independently change the task-outcome classifications."]}
